,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":70.196726215,"data":"[Question] Expand $(2z^2 + 5z - 6)(3z^3 - 2z + 1)$.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":70.196753276,"data":"[Answer 1] \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":70.196760422,"data":"\\begin{aligned} (2z^2 + 5z - 6)(3z^3 - 2z + 1) \u0026= 2z^2(3z^3 - 2z + 1) + 5z(3z^3 - 2z + 1) - 6(3z^3 - 2z + 1) \\\\ \u0026= 6z^5 - 4z^3 + 2z^2 + 15z^4 - 10z^2 + 5z - 18z^3 + 12z - 6 \\\\ \u0026= 6z^5 + 15z^4 - 22z^3 - 10z^2 + 12z - 6 \\end{aligned} \\boxed{6z^5 + 15z^4 - 22z^3 - 10z^2 + 12z - 6}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":70.196767635,"data":"[Answer 2] \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":70.19677407,"data":"First, we need to expand the product \\((2z^2 + 5z - 6)(3z^3 - 2z + 1)\\). We will use the distributive property (also known as the FOIL method for binomials or the distributive property for polynomials). \\[ (2z^2 + 5z - 6)(3z^3 - 2z + 1) \\] We distribute each term in the first polynomial to each term in the second polynomial: \\[ 2z^2 \\cdot 3z^3 + 2z^2 \\cdot (-2z) + 2z^2 \\cdot 1 + 5z \\cdot 3z^3 + 5z \\cdot (-2z) + 5z \\cdot 1 - 6 \\cdot 3z^3 - 6 \\cdot (-2z) - 6 \\cdot 1 \\] Now, we compute each term: \\[ 2z^2 \\cdot 3z^3 = 6z^5 \\] \\[ 2z^2 \\cdot (-2z) = -4z^3 \\] \\[ 2z^2 \\cdot 1 = 2z^2 \\] \\[ 5z \\cdot 3z^3 = 15z^4 \\] \\[ 5z \\cdot (-2z) = -10z^2 \\] \\[ 5z \\cdot 1 = 5z \\] \\[ -6 \\cdot 3z^3 = -18z^3 \\] \\[ -6 \\cdot (-2z) = 12z \\] \\[ -6 \\cdot 1 = -6 \\] Now, we combine all these terms: \\[ 6z^5 - 4z^3 + 2z^2 + 15z^4 - 10z^2 + 5z - 18z^3 + 12z - 6 \\] Combine like terms: \\[ 6z^5 + 15z^4 + (-4z^3 - 18z^3) + (2z^2 - 10z^2) + 5z + 12z - 6 \\] \\[ 6z^5 + 15z^4 - 22z^3 - 8z^2 + 17z - 6 \\] So, the expanded form is: \\[ \\boxed{6z^5 + 15z^4 - 22z^3 - 8z^2 + 17z - 6} \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":70.19679899,"data":"[Refined answer] \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":70.196805031,"data":"To expand the expression \\((2z^2 + 5z - 6)(3z^3 - 2z + 1)\\), we distribute each term of the first polynomial to each term of the second polynomial. First, distribute \\(2z^2\\) across the second polynomial: \\[2z^2 \\cdot 3z^3 = 6z^5\\] \\[2z^2 \\cdot (-2z) = -4z^3\\] \\[2z^2 \\cdot 1 = 2z^2\\] Next, distribute \\(5z\\) across the second polynomial: \\[5z \\cdot 3z^3 = 15z^4\\] \\[5z \\cdot (-2z) = -10z^2\\] \\[5z \\cdot 1 = 5z\\] Finally, distribute \\(-6\\) across the second polynomial: \\[-6 \\cdot 3z^3 = -18z^3\\] \\[-6 \\cdot (-2z) = 12z\\] \\[-6 \\cdot 1 = -6\\] Now, combine all these terms together: \\[6z^5 - 4z^3 + 2z^2 + 15z^4 - 10z^2 + 5z - 18z^3 + 12z - 6\\] Combine like terms: \\[6z^5 + 15z^4 + (-4z^3 - 18z^3) + (2z^2 - 10z^2) + (5z + 12z) - 6\\] Simplify further: \\[6z^5 + 15z^4 - 22z^3 - 8z^2 + 17z - 6\\] Thus, the expanded form of \\((2z^2 + 5z - 6)(3z^3 - 2z + 1)\\) is \\[6z^5 + 15z^4 - 22z^3 - 8z^2 + 17z - 6\\] \\[ \\boxed{6z^5 + 15z^4 - 22z^3 - 8z^2 + 17z - 6} \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":70.196814736,"data":"[Final answer] 6z^5 + 15z^4 - 22z^3 - 8z^2 + 17z - 6\u003c|endoftext|\u003e\n"}
